WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.460
The eight long, pointed legs of a massive&nbsp;
spider, fangs dripping with deadly venom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:10.080
skitter across the ground. It is one&nbsp;
of the apex predators here… Until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:16.560
it’s crushed by the scaly foot of SCP-682,&nbsp;
the Backrooms’ newest, angriest resident.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:22.920
When we last left our least favorite anomalous&nbsp;
reptile, SCP-682 was eight levels deep into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:28.920
terrifying extra-dimensional labyrinth known&nbsp;
as The Backrooms. With SCP-343 knows how many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.780
levels left to traverse, the hard-to-destroy&nbsp;
reptile was beginning to feel a bubbling sense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:40.920
of contempt for everything in this godforsaken&nbsp;
reality. That is to say, SCP-682 felt the way it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:46.380
usually felt, but for once, there were no feeble&nbsp;
Foundation personnel to unleash its rage on.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.320
And while its long absence&nbsp;
back in the world outside of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:54.120
The Backrooms has been seen as a stressful&nbsp;
inconvenience for most of The Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:59.700
the fact that the keter-class creature had done&nbsp;
no further harm since it evaded containment had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:07.020
led many researchers to believe that, however&nbsp;
unlikely it was: SCP-682 no longer existed.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.320
“It’s out of our hair!” said one Dr. Wazowski.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:13.740
Though the Foundation would continue to&nbsp;
launch around-the-clock reconnaissance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:18.540
missions the world over, the Mobile Task Force&nbsp;
that seemingly did the deed of destroying the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:22.260
hard-to-destroy reptile was currently&nbsp;
being treated to a company pizza party&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:26.880
paid for by The Foundation’s “Sorry A&nbsp;
Lizard Ate Your Loved One” Fund which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:32.580
received a small donation from the O-5 Council&nbsp;
every time that SCP-682 breached containment.

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:37.680
But there was no chance of relief for&nbsp;
SCP-682 itself, as wandering through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:43.440
The Backrooms without a map or strong sense of&nbsp;
purpose was certainly no pizza party. Level 8,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:49.380
the level that SCP-682 currently found itself&nbsp;
on, was a cave system crawling with all manner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:55.440
of hostile entities. Well, hostile for weak and&nbsp;
pathetic human beings at least. To say the same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.440 --> 00:02:01.740
was true for SCP-682 would be a gross distortion&nbsp;
of the definition of the word hostile, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:07.800
because SCP-682 had faced many of these miserable&nbsp;
monstrosities before on the previous levels.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:14.340
The Clumps, Hounds, Death Rats, and Smilers were&nbsp;
back in droves, and these now all too familiar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:20.040
entities seemingly couldn’t help themselves&nbsp;
from aggressively pouncing on SCP-682 the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.780
second that the reptile entered their line of&nbsp;
sight. Not that getting the drop on the anomaly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:30.900
would buy them any advantage, as SCP-682&nbsp;
effortlessly bodied them one after another.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.760
Playing the hits already,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:39.420
Backrooms? SCP-682 thought to itself. At&nbsp;
least give me something new to chew on.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:45.960
Through the jumble of stalactites and stalagmites,&nbsp;
SCP-682 could see a child faceling standing on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:51.780
the other side of an unusual pit of tar. The&nbsp;
last time that SCP-682 encountered a few of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:57.000
these unfittingly named faceless little girls&nbsp;
during its time on Level 2, it had ignored the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:01.680
entities out of a sense that there would be more&nbsp;
interesting monsters to destroy going forward.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:09.180
SCP-682 now realized, almost shamefully, that it&nbsp;
had largely been proven wrong. Perhaps the child&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:14.520
facelings were in fact more than meets the eye,&nbsp;
or knew something that the other entities didn’t.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:20.820
Regardless, there were never enough pathetic&nbsp;
cretins in The Backrooms for SCP-682 to vent its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:27.360
nigh-limitless frustration on. The small faceling&nbsp;
would simply be the next to bite the dust. Or so,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:32.520
SCP-682 thought. As the hard-to-destroy&nbsp;
reptile charged towards the entity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:36.600
its claws touched down on the puddle&nbsp;
of tar, and almost immediately:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:42.540
a countless number of human hands emerged from&nbsp;
the liquid beneath and pulled SCP-682 under.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:46.980
The anomaly was able to easily adapt the&nbsp;
level of strength necessary to escape from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:51.240
the grasp of the tar pit entities and&nbsp;
resurface. When it emerged, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:57.180
the child faceling was nowhere to be found.&nbsp;
SCP-682 had to give the creepy little menace some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:02.100
credit as it was apparently smarter than the other&nbsp;
entities which had crossed the lizard’s path.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:07.860
SCP-682 put as much distance between itself&nbsp;
and that annoying tar pit as it could,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:12.840
and it was vigilant for any other similar&nbsp;
hazards. Not especially amused by the concept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:18.900
of being swallowed up again, SCP-682 adapted a&nbsp;
pair of large draconic wings which it used to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:23.280
carry itself aloft through the caves of Level&nbsp;
8. From above, the anomaly could see a number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:28.500
of foot-long centipede-like entities as well as&nbsp;
entities that resembled eyeless chickens, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:35.340
for once, neither of these horrendous mistakes of&nbsp;
creation seemed interested in assaulting SCP-682.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:42.420
It was surprising, but SCP-682 actually felt a&nbsp;
little bit relieved. Not because it felt remotely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:46.860
threatened by anything that crawled, trotted, or&nbsp;
slunk through The Backrooms, but because it didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:51.360
have to waste any of its valuable time putting&nbsp;
down another weakling that should know better.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:56.160
This relief was short-lived as all of&nbsp;
a sudden, a large shape dropped down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.160 --> 00:05:02.880
on SCP-682 from the ceiling. This monstrous&nbsp;
humanoid boasted four powerful limbs and was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:08.100
currently using all of them in an attempt&nbsp;
to pummel SCP-682 back down to the ground.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:13.680
SCP-682 could see several similar entities&nbsp;
emerging from the nearby cavern walls, having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:18.840
apparently blended in through color-changing&nbsp;
camouflage and lying completely still in wait&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:24.960
for prey or in the case of SCP-682, the&nbsp;
anomalous lizard that would prey on them.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:30.000
These entities are called Camo Crawlers&nbsp;
by the Major Explorer Group, and because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.980
they have the same level of intelligence as&nbsp;
regular humans and cooperate to hunt in packs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:41.100
they are regarded as one of the more difficult&nbsp;
entities to deal with. Not for SCP-682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:47.040
of course, and the hateful beast could not be more&nbsp;
disappointed in this latest ill-conceived ambush.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:53.580
SCP-682 came to a landing on part of the cavern&nbsp;
floor which was decidedly not covered with tar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:59.100
and allowed its wings to retract back into its&nbsp;
body. Without a moment to spare, it quickly made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:05.280
short work of the Camo Crawlers. The lot of them&nbsp;
may have been as smart as humans, but SCP-682&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:11.100
had killed a lot of humans in its time, and an&nbsp;
extra pair of arms wasn’t exactly a game-changer.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:17.520
Now surrounded by a record number of expired&nbsp;
Backrooms entities, SCP-682 realized it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.300
growing sick of Level 8. It seemed that&nbsp;
there was no winning with this place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:26.640
as the levels that SCP-682 had visited&nbsp;
previously either contained hordes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:31.920
worthless expendable fodder like this one or&nbsp;
were so empty that the SCP would find itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:37.680
longing for any kind of interaction. It was&nbsp;
time to search for an exit to this level with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:43.680
the hope that the next inconceivably vast maze of&nbsp;
nothingness had a more refreshing flavor to it.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:48.420
Knowing the Backrooms, the exit to Level 8 would&nbsp;
probably come in the form of an off-color portion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:54.060
of cave wall or some glitched geometry straight&nbsp;
out of those video games that younger humans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.060 --> 00:07:00.000
seem to love to play. Fortunately, SCP-682&nbsp;
didn’t have to think too hard about how to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.540
progress to the next level, as after&nbsp;
wandering around for long enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:08.040
it merely fell straight through a random&nbsp;
section of the floor into darkness.

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:13.500
Seconds later, SCP-682 appeared in&nbsp;
the lamppost-lit streets of Level 9:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:17.760
also known as the infinite suburb.&nbsp;
It looked close to midnight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:23.460
and much like in Micheal Jackson’s hit song&nbsp;
Thriller, evil things were no doubt lurking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:28.440
in the dark. But none eviler than&nbsp;
the hard-to-destroy reptile itself.

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:33.960
If Level 9 was anything like the suburbs that&nbsp;
SCP-682 remembered from its native reality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:39.420
this place should be filled with humans packed&nbsp;
together like sardines in a can. And while the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:45.060
lucky Foundation Mobile Task Force that was&nbsp;
present at the site SCP-682 had no-clipped into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:52.200
The Backrooms at were likely enjoying some sardine&nbsp;
pizza for a job well done, SCP-682 was fixing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:58.020
make the next humans it encountered into its&nbsp;
own kind of unconventional topping for a feast.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:03.000
It was feeling oddly rejuvenated and&nbsp;
almost happy again, and what it didn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:07.800
know was that the darkness of Level 9&nbsp;
had the same anomalous - or I suppose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:14.160
vaguely supernatural - properties of Level&nbsp;
6. And as the research suggests, many kinds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:20.880
of emotional inversion fields that unnerve and&nbsp;
disturb ordinary humans make SCP-682 feel the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:28.020
opposite way. It was strange, but somehow SCP-682&nbsp;
felt almost like it belonged here in Suburbia.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:31.980
Just a little old me in a big big world.

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:36.780
SCP-682 mused to itself, before&nbsp;
trotting down the pavement through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:39.780
the neighborhood. Its mouth was&nbsp;
starting to water as it carefully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.780 --> 00:08:43.980
deliberated over which of these sleepy&nbsp;
community homes it would enter first.

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:48.720
The idea that behind every door there were&nbsp;
unsuspecting humans fresh for the slaughter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:54.240
made this place seem like paradise for the&nbsp;
reptile. This rare good mood even remained as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.240 --> 00:09:01.020
a new group of quote-unquote “hostile entities”&nbsp;
made their way down the street towards SCP-682.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:04.920
Alright then, let’s meet the welcoming committee.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:10.200
These entities were known as The Neighborhood&nbsp;
Watch, and the most relatively interesting thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:15.360
about their appearance was that their anatomy&nbsp;
seemed to be centered around singularly massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:21.120
eyeballs. Without hesitation, one of the&nbsp;
cyclopean entities, a floating eyeball known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:27.780
as a “Watcher” fired a piercing ray of light at&nbsp;
SCP-682, which instantly disintegrated portions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:32.760
of the reptile’s body on contact. Unlike the&nbsp;
corrosive acid used by the death moths and the&nbsp;

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:40.560
bursters from Level 5, the damage inflicted&nbsp;
on SCP-682 was at the atomic level.

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:45.060
What this effectively meant is that the&nbsp;
regeneration time to recover from these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:49.920
injuries was going to be slightly longer than&nbsp;
usual. The other advantage that The Watchers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:54.720
had was strength in numbers, as there were&nbsp;
three of them, as well as a pair of “Striders”:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:59.820
ambulatory eyeballs on 8-foot legs which&nbsp;
brought up the rear of The Neighborhood Watch.

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:04.140
“Two can play at that game!” said SCP-682.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:09.900
It instantly copied The Watcher’s disintegration&nbsp;
rays, firing a pair of atomic lasers from both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:15.120
eyes that would make a superhuman blush. These&nbsp;
lasers of heat and light hit their marks with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:19.920
perfect accuracy and dismantled the particles of&nbsp;
the entire approaching The Neighborhood Watch.

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:23.640
As per usual, The Backrooms then&nbsp;
proceeded to roll out the usual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:29.220
clown car of stooges. SCP-682 could see&nbsp;
Death Moths, a couple Skin Stealers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:34.860
and some particularly wretched Wretches&nbsp;
hiding among the suburban homes. The reptile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:39.240
made a sport of using its newly adapted&nbsp;
laser-vision to pick them off one by one.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:42.120
Zap!! I see you! Zap!

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:48.000
Before long, there were no more Backrooms entities&nbsp;
in sight, and SCP-682 decided that it was time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:54.360
to break into one of the houses on the street&nbsp;
and go to town. Or technically, go to suburbia.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:58.620
Honey, I’m home! SCP-682 thought to itself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:00.960
as smashed through the front&nbsp;
door of one of the buildings.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:07.980
Inside was no trace of habitation: no food,&nbsp;
no photographs, and absolutely no humans.&nbsp;

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:14.760
Oh well. Thought 682, still mellowed out from the&nbsp;
effects of the darkness. There’s always next door.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:17.280
It exited through the hole in the wall it made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:20.460
and strode across the lawn to the&nbsp;
next little house on the square.

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:21.840
Knock knock!

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:27.840
SCP-682 burst in once more, and found this&nbsp;
house to be in much the same state as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:34.380
last. Undaunted and feeling persistent, SCP-682&nbsp;
made its way down the street like a terrifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:39.000
door-to-door salesman: busting through&nbsp;
the front door of every house in its path.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:39.960
Telegram!

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:41.460
Special delivery!

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:44.040
I’m here to talk to you about car insurance!

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:53.100
There was nothing. No humans anywhere. Level 9&nbsp;
seemed to be one big empty ghost town. SCP-682&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:58.380
started to consider the implications of the number&nbsp;
of entities it had encountered earlier. While they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:03.960
were little more than distractions for SCP-682,&nbsp;
the chances were very slim that any humans that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:08.760
had made it this far could have survived&nbsp;
such a plethora of dime store goofballs.
 &nbsp;

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:13.080
SCP-682 let out an&nbsp;
uncharacteristically wistful sigh.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:16.800
The Backrooms got me all messed&nbsp;
up. I can’t believe I’m actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:21.660
missing those disgusting humans. I’ve&nbsp;
grown accustomed to their faces. 
 &nbsp;

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:27.120
SCP-682 reflected on this for a moment&nbsp;
and then had another realization.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:33.120
No, this is perfect. I’m free! I may&nbsp;
never see those worthless creatures again!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:38.760
They’ll never inflict their pathetic&nbsp;
existence on what is mine. I am free!

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:45.120
SCP-682 howled in private triumphant victory&nbsp;
as it rambled through the streets of this dead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:51.840
world unknown to humans and especially unknown to&nbsp;
The Foundation. This was nothing like the endless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:58.320
office space of Level 4, because the darkness&nbsp;
negated any possible depression that SCP-682&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:03.240
could develop as a result of being deprived&nbsp;
of other entities to interact with. Even then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:10.140
it was clear that there would be more than enough&nbsp;
entities for SCP-682 to destroy if it got bored.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:15.000
While there was no telling how often entities&nbsp;
in The Backrooms spawn or where they really come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:21.180
from, there never seemed to be a shortage in&nbsp;
the levels where they did exist. SCP-682 began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:27.180
to think that Level 9 was in fact the paradise it&nbsp;
appeared to be at first glance. Against all odds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:33.720
SCP-682 had achieved genuine bliss, and it&nbsp;
seemed that nothing could take that away.

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:39.720
As SCP-682 stood there staring up into&nbsp;
the starless black void of Level 9’s sky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:43.860
it was caught off guard by the sudden&nbsp;
presence of what appeared to be a blue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:49.500
hyacinth macaw landing on its back. The bird&nbsp;
had given no indication that it was nearby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:56.460
and because of that, it had somehow taken&nbsp;
SCP-682 completely by surprise. What’s more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.460 --> 00:14:01.800
the reptile was feeling an unusual&nbsp;
sensation within its mind. It knew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:06.960
almost instinctively, that this avian entity’s&nbsp;
name was Jerry and also that it was one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:12.180
only beings SCP-682 had ever encountered&nbsp;
that it didn’t outright want to destroy.

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:19.020
It wasn’t that SCP-682 liked Jerry or even&nbsp;
really cared if he lived or died, but there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:23.040
was something about this unusual macaw&nbsp;
that didn’t trigger the usual disgust&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:27.420
response that every other form of&nbsp;
life brought out in SCP-682. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:32.340
wasn’t admiration or friendship, but&nbsp;
more like… optimistic indifference.

00:14:32.340 --> 00:14:38.220
“Your existence is acceptable, Jerry,”&nbsp;
said SCP-682 to its newfound winged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:41.100
companion. “Let’s go find some weaklings to kill.”

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:44.280
“Squawk! Weaklings!” Jerry replied.

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:50.580
And so SCP-682 was off again, this time with Jerry&nbsp;
in tow. It was the two of them against the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:57.840
and together, they could take on anything. SCP-682&nbsp;
and Jerry out on adventures! Running around and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:03.840
accomplishing great things in The Backrooms!&nbsp;
One hundred years of SCP-682 and Jerry! 
 &nbsp;

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:09.780
Eventually, the asphalt and suburban houses gave&nbsp;
way to an unpaved dirt path leading through a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:14.820
field of wheat. Within moments, the darkness was&nbsp;
replaced with a dense fog, and the black of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:20.940
night sky changed into the gray of a cloudy&nbsp;
afternoon. SCP-682 breathed in the moist air,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:26.100
and realized that once again, it had moved between&nbsp;
levels of The Backrooms without knowing it.

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:30.480
This was Level 10, the infinite&nbsp;
wheat field. At this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:33.240
the word infinite was starting to feel cheap.

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:37.620
“Some warning would have&nbsp;
been nice,” SCP-682 grumbled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:41.760
no longer feeling as serene without&nbsp;
the benefits of Level 9’s darkness.

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:45.660
At least Jerry was still here. There&nbsp;
was a silver lining to everything.

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:46.860
No!

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:52.380
SCP-682 stomped its feet on the ground in&nbsp;
building frustration. It needed to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:57.360
something to tear to pieces immediately, or it&nbsp;
might reconsider even its tolerance of Jerry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.360 --> 00:16:01.860
The macaw was now its last resort in case&nbsp;
there were no other entities on this Level.

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:07.920
Fortunately for Jerry, SCP-682 became alerted&nbsp;
by the echoing sounds of trumpets coming from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:13.020
further into the wheat field and decided to&nbsp;
investigate. Through the mists of Level 10,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:20.820
SCP-682 could see the silhouettes of several&nbsp;
large stone towers. SCP-682 didn’t recognize the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:25.320
exact time period of the architecture, the way a&nbsp;
human might assume they were from the middle ages,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:30.060
but it could definitely tell that these were&nbsp;
old. It hadn’t destroyed something like this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:34.620
in ages, and it seemed as though&nbsp;
it would soon be given a reason to.

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:39.480
Perched high on the towers were a small&nbsp;
patrol of goblinoid creatures wielding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:45.300
bows and arrows. These entities spotted&nbsp;
SCP-682 around the same time it spotted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:49.800
them and began to nock arrows from their&nbsp;
quivers and open fire relentlessly on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:54.540
reptile. These ancient projectiles stung,&nbsp;
but compared to the disintegration rays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:59.100
from the Watchers, SCP-682 saw&nbsp;
this as a bit of a downgrade.

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:04.260
The only real harm that it did to&nbsp;
SCP-682 was spiritual, as the rain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:09.480
of arrows seemed to startle Jerry and cause&nbsp;
the macaw to take flight away from SCP-682.

00:17:09.480 --> 00:17:12.300
“Jerry!! Get back here, you coward!!”

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:17.820
SCP-682 shouted to the birdlike entity as it&nbsp;
disappeared from sight. It shook its head.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.820 --> 00:17:23.940
However brief it was, it seemed that the&nbsp;
682 and Jerry team-up had come to an end.

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:27.840
Stupid bird. He better hope I don’t see him again.

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:31.800
The Archers continued to&nbsp;
pepper SCP-682 with arrows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:36.360
but the reptile wasn’t about to take medieval&nbsp;
warfare lying down. With extreme speed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:42.540
SCP-682 charged at the nearest tower and rammed&nbsp;
it head-on. The impact shook the structure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:47.880
causing the archers to stumble and drop some&nbsp;
of their arrows. Despite the damage, the tower&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:54.120
hadn’t fully crumbled, so SCP-682 underwent&nbsp;
a brand new adaptation to settle the score.

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:59.640
Armored plates converged at the end of&nbsp;
SCP-682’s tail, forming a large bludgeoning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:05.280
club similar to that of an ankylosaurus. With&nbsp;
the power and speed of 682’s body behind it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:09.300
this bony mass was more accurately&nbsp;
described as a wrecking ball.

00:18:09.300 --> 00:18:14.580
And it came in like a wrecking ball, too,&nbsp;
as the reptile swung its whole body with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:19.320
enough force to smash the base of the&nbsp;
tower into pieces. As the stone fell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:23.940
so did the archers, and many were buried&nbsp;
beneath the rubble while others scattered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:28.140
retreating to farther towers&nbsp;
while taking pot shots at SCP-682.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:34.380
The reptile didn’t chase them. It had bigger&nbsp;
plans. It waited until the archers had made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:39.240
their way into the next few towers before&nbsp;
grabbing a piece of rubble in its mouth and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:44.820
chucking it directly up into the air. The&nbsp;
chunk of stone flew upwards and then began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:49.500
to descend rapidly towards the wheat field&nbsp;
below. Demonstrating an eye for precision&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:55.740
on par with the siege engineers of medieval&nbsp;
times, SCP-682 swung its club tail at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:55.740 --> 00:19:01.500
perfect moment to hit the falling stone&nbsp;
and change its course. It was a home run!

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:07.560
SCP-682 scored a direct hit on the top of the&nbsp;
next tower, and repeated its stone-chucking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:12.120
strategy until the Archers began to get&nbsp;
the message. This was a war the likes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:17.460
which these Freddy-Freaker-looking demons had&nbsp;
never experienced. The hard-to-destroy reptile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:21.960
roared a blustering battle cry and began&nbsp;
to berate the entities for their weakness.

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:28.980
“You miscreants deserve this for scaring Jerry&nbsp;
away!” SCP-682 said without really thinking.

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:34.620
What had gotten into it? Some strange anomalous&nbsp;
effect? It pondered this as it continued to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:39.120
perform its rather convincing impression of&nbsp;
a catapult. The archers had completely taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:43.500
cover at this point, afraid to retaliate&nbsp;
for fear of getting a rock to the face.

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:48.840
Not too long after, the same trumpet noise could&nbsp;
be heard again, and the area around the towers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:55.140
became a lot less active. It did take SCP-682 a&nbsp;
moment or two to realize that the entities had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:55.140 --> 00:20:01.020
all disappeared with the sound of that instrument.&nbsp;
Cowards would be cowards, after all. The reptile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:01.020 --> 00:20:05.940
was aching for more of a fight, but at the very&nbsp;
least, Level 10 was offering something new.

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:12.960
Though not all of it was new. A Smiler peeked&nbsp;
out at SCP-682 from between stocks of wheat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:17.340
and this time the reptile simply chose&nbsp;
to ignore the uncanny grinning bastard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:17.340 --> 00:20:21.180
and move on. No sense giving&nbsp;
it the satisfaction, right?

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:26.880
SCP-682 followed the dirt path for about a&nbsp;
day, during which time it also encountered a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:32.160
pack of hounds, a skin-stealer, and who could&nbsp;
say how many death rats that scampered amidst&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:36.780
the field. After all this, it came to what&nbsp;
appeared to be some kind of settlement. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:36.780 --> 00:20:42.000
buildings here looked much more modern than the&nbsp;
towers, and unlike the empty suburbs of Level 9,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:45.720
the reptile could see that there&nbsp;
were actual humans living here.

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:50.280
From all appearances, this appeared to be a&nbsp;
small town square with an open-air trading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:55.560
post much like a farmer’s market. In addition&nbsp;
to wheat, the humans living in this settlement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:55.560 --> 00:21:00.360
had all sorts of goods on display and could&nbsp;
be seen actively bartering with each other.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:06.900
SCP-682 licked its lips. None of those helpless&nbsp;
fools knew that it was coming. Malt Town,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:10.860
as it was known to wanderers in The&nbsp;
Backrooms, was about to receive a rude&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:15.480
awakening at the hands of a keter-class&nbsp;
SCP. While the archers that had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:19.920
encountered earlier posed a definite threat&nbsp;
to those straying too close to their towers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:24.360
the entities seemed to conveniently&nbsp;
ignore this humble little town.

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:31.320
Of course, mercy was not in SCP-682’s playbook.&nbsp;
Except for when it came to Jerry, apparently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:38.400
but the macaw was gone now, and it was&nbsp;
time for carnage. This was going to be fun.

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:44.460
go check out “Could SCP-682 be Contained&nbsp;
in the Backrooms?” and “SCP-682 Slaughters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:46.920
Through the Backrooms” for more Backrooms carnage!

